      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(openai-http): keep SSE argument chunking UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nSSE streaming chunks split tool-call JSON arguments at 256 code-unit boundaries. When a surrogate pair (emoji, CJK) straddles the boundary, both chunks contain unpaired surrogates, producing invalid JSON fragments in the SSE stream.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe existing `String.prototype.slice()` operates on UTF-16 code units and can split surrogate pairs. Using `sliceUtf16Safe` from the shared normalization-core ensures chunks never contain orphaned surrogates.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers sending tool-call arguments containing emoji or supplementary-plane characters may receive corrupt SSE chunks when arguments exceed 256 code units.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAll 40 tests passed (gateway-client suite: 20/20 passed; gateway-server suite had 1 pre-existing failure unrelated to this change: \"gateway method handler is missing a descriptor: conversations.list\").\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n",
        "branch": "fix/openai-http-utf16-slice",
